On Sep 6, 4:25 pm, funcrunch <web-goog...@funcrunch.org> wrote:
> I disagree with this strategy. I much prefer to save prayer for
> emergencies other than starvation.

I used to feel this way, but it started to seem to me that any other
emergency I didn't have some other way out of would probably kill me
even after I got something as nice as a complete healing from the
deity.

There are real exceptions to that rule, so the pattern that's seemed
to work for me is to use prayer to build up food early, before I'm
likely to run into any emergencies, and then only use prayer if my
stash seems low. Typically this translates to never eating the first
two pieces of significant food I find unless I have no other choice.
This way hunger rarely becomes an emergency, and just stays another
game choice.






